# TypeScript

- Strict. No `any`. Unknown input is `unknown`, then parse with Zod (`src/features/<domain>/schema`). Infer with `z.infer<typeof schema>` — do not duplicate unions.
- Prefer `type` for unions/props; `interface` only when you must extend (Mongoose `Document` types are fine).
- Named exports. Files are kebab-case (`create-booking.service.ts`). React components PascalCase in kebab files (`step1-trip-details.tsx` → `export function Step1TripDetails`).
- No default exports except Next.js `page.tsx` / `layout.tsx` / `route.ts` and Mongoose model files that already default-export.
- Functions do one job. Name with a verb: `calculateBookingPrice`, `finalizePaidBooking`.
- Don't swallow errors.

```ts
// BAD
} catch (e) {}

// GOOD
} catch (error) {
  throw new Error("Failed to create booking", { cause: error });
}
```

- Dates/money: `Intl` with the active locale. Don't concatenate currency by hand.
- Avoid barrel files that re-export entire modules. Re-export only a folder's public surface (`src/features/booking/model/index.ts`). Auth may export `authOptions` from `@/features/auth` (server only).
